class_name MotionTable
extends RefCounted
## GENERATED by tools/gen_motion_table.gd: do not edit by hand, run that (the commands are in its header) to measure it again.
## How the coarse motion of long steps behaves, measured from the real run-and-tumble swimming: the drift up the nutrient
## gradient and the diffusion along and across it, as a function of s (speed times the log-gradient the swimmer faces) and
## eps (the error in its estimate of it). SimCore reads these from SimConstants.build() and loads them into the
## dish tables (the motion_* slots of gpu/gpu_layout.gd). The two hashes say what it was measured from; MotionFingerprint and the tests compare them.
## Made from the average of independent runs of the generator's ramp set, one per seed (700 runs: seeds 1001-1560 on Direct3D 12; seeds 1-40, 201-300 on Metal). Drift: the
## measured average where s > 0.01 or eps < 0.03; where s <= 0.01 and eps >= 0.03, a straight line through zero in s, k(eps) * s,
## with k fitted to the average of the rows there, non-increasing in eps and smooth (tools/gen_motion_table.gd, _fit).
## A cell that fell below the one before it by no more than noise is set equal to it; the declines past the drift's peak at
## high s and low eps are measured and kept.
## Row-major: the value for S_AXIS[i] and E_AXIS[j] is at index i * E_AXIS.size() + j.
